{"id": "EUVD-2026-104679", "enisaUuid": "3130f1fa-fb58-3b03-b5a6-732193ba8e80", "description": "Ning compress-lzf before 1.2.0 contains an out-of-bounds memory access vulnerability in the sun.misc.Unsafe based UnsafeChunkDecoder that fails to validate back-references and literal runs. Attackers can supply crafted LZF streams to applications using the default LZFDecoder to leak unrelated JVM heap memory into decompressed output or crash the JVM.", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T00:46:04", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T14:29:50", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/ning/compress/pull/68", "https://github.com/ning/compress/commit/06bdc3744a96b736a7118891f403e44c664f108b", "https://github.com/ning/compress/blob/compress-lzf-1.1.3/src/main/java/com/ning/compress/lzf/impl/UnsafeChunkDecoder.java#L104", "https://github.com/github/securitylab/discussions/970", "https://github.com/ning/compress", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ning-compress-lzf-before-1.2.0-out-of-bounds-memory-access-via-unsafechunkdecoder"], "aliases": ["GHSA-7xjc-8h6q-2f5h", "CVE-2026-109395"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.4, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1b9c5c1d-18af-34db-b06a-60466112b8a6", "product": {"name": "compress-lzf", "vendor": {"name": "ning"}}, "product_version": "0 <1.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "41c72fdd-4b4e-364d-96f7-f8c40334c230", "vendor": {"name": "ning"}}], "isExploited": false}